# Website / OCR backlog (do not memory-hole)

Before any website, OCR, diocese viewer, parish page, mega-PDF, or `docs/` HTML work:

1. Read `docs/WEBSITE_OCR_BACKLOG.md` and update it when you add or finish an item.
2. Do **not** mark an item done unless you verified it on **generated** HTML/CSS (`docs/dioceses/`, `docs/parishes/`, `docs/bulletins/`, or a fresh `render_bulletin_viewer_shell` render). Python-only changes disappear on the next harvest.
3. Desktop PDF **and** OCR panels: **locked** `height` / `min-height` / `max-height` **850px**. Mobile/tablet (`max-width: 1024px`): **locked 450px**. Extra PDF/OCR content scrolls **inside** the box (`overflow: auto`). Do **not** use `height: auto` or `85vh` so the page grows for metres. Keep `#scroll-top-btn` for jumping to the top of the **page**. Keep sticky search **outside** `#ocr-panel` (`.ocr-sticky-chrome` sibling above it). Put this in `render_bulletin_viewer_shell` (canonical generator), then regenerate live diocese pages. `docs/assets/pdf-inpage-viewer.js` `ensureStyles()` must lock the same 850/450 with `!important`.
4. OCR must show a parish name header, real section headings (promote existing Mass times / Anniversaries / notices / fundraising / contact lines — do not invent events), and professional spacing. Keep Irish/Gaeilge as Irish.
5. Parish and diocese links open in a new tab (`target="_blank"` `rel="noopener noreferrer"`). Mega-PDF header URLs must work in the in-page PDF.js viewer (annotation overlay), not only in a downloaded PDF.
6. Mega PDF generation stays on. Do not disable `HARVEST_MEGA_PDF`.
